    "result_text": "All 25 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` derived field on the Owner response, following the existing pattern used for other derived read-only fields (`displayName`, `initials`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema (the `OwnerDto` is code-generated from this spec at build time).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression to `toOwnerDto` that computes the tier: `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`. The condition guards against nulls (`namesakeCount != null`, `email != null && !email.isEmpty()`), so a missing count or empty email yields `BRONZE`.\n\nThe logic reuses the already-persisted `namesakeCount` (set at create time in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`) and the owner's email, so the tier is derived consistently on every read. Both new Cp15 tests (SILVER with unique name + email; BRONZE with no email) and all 23 pre-existing tests pass.",
